    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d974">

                <pb facs="1034" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1024"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.119/8–2249</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Director of the Executive Secretariat</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">McWilliams</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Deputy Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Rusk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-08-22">August 22, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Webb<anchor n="52" xml:id="d974-f1"/> has read the attached<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d974-f2"/> but is not convinced that the recommended course is the
                    proper one. He says that Admiral Hillen-koetter<anchor n="54" xml:id="d974-f3"/>
                    informs him that the quantities are serious and that the President has
                    previously stated that he wants to make things just as tough economically for
                    the Chinese Communists as is possible.</p>
                <p>In view of the above, would you please have this reexamined to see if the answer
                    is the same?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">McWilliams</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d974-f1" n="52" xml:id="d974-f1-content">
                <p>James E. Webb, Under Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d974-f2" n="53" xml:id="d974-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d974-f3" n="54" xml:id="d974-f3-content">
                <p>Rear Adm. R. H. Hillenkoetter, Director of Central Intelligence.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
